name: sim.reorientShapeBoundingBox
description:
luaSynopsis: int result=sim.reorientShapeBoundingBox(int shapeHandle,int relativeToHandle)
pythonSynopsis: int result=sim.reorientShapeBoundingBox(int shapeHandle,int relativeToHandle)
inputs (possibly taken/adapted from C-function counterpart. Adjust accordingly):
1. shapeHandle: the handle of the shape that will be reoriented. See also sim.getObject.
2. relativeToHandle: the handle of an object relative to which the shape should be reoriented, or -1 to align the bounding box with the world, or sim.handle_self to build the smallest bounding box around the object.
3. reservedSetToZero: reserved for future extensions. Set to 0.
outputs (possibly taken/adapted from C-function counterpart. Adjust accordingly):
1. -1 if operation was not successful. 0 if the bounding box could not be reoriented (the bounding box of primitive shapes cannot be reoriented), otherwise 1.
replacedBy:
- name: alignBoundingBox, class: shape, file: shape_alignBoundingBox.method
